# Atlas AI — environment template
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill real values.
# NEVER commit real keys. Source of truth: ~/Desktop/api/KEYS.md.

# ---------------------- Supabase (P1 + P2) ----------------------
# Created in P1 — Supabase project in region ap-southeast-1 (Singapore).
# This is an accepted deviation from PRD §6 target of ap-southeast-2 (Sydney) — Sam override.
# Full audit trail: planning/atlas-ai/DEVIATIONS.md §DEV-001.
# APP 8 cross-border disclosure is live in the lead-capture APP 5 notice (Phase 3).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...  # anon key — safe for client
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...       # server-side only, NEVER to client

# ---------------------- OpenAI (P5) ----------------------
# P5 migrates from OpenRouter free-tier to OpenAI production.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---------------------- OpenRouter (legacy demo chat — P5 retires) ----------------------
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# ---------------------- Resend (P3) ----------------------
# Transactional email — lead notifications to Sam + UniMate.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
LEAD_NOTIFY_EMAILS=sam@claudeking.org,{unimate-ops-email-TBD}

# ---------------------- Deployment ----------------------
# Used in system prompts + metadata.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://atlas-ai.vercel.app

# ---------------------- N8N lead-sync (DORMANT v1 add-on — see PRD §3 X.1.1) ----------------------
# Atlas AI ships with a ready-to-deploy N8N workflow at ops/n8n/lead-sync-workflow.json
# that mirrors new leads to a Google Sheet via Supabase Database Webhooks.
# NOT active in v1 core delivery. Activation is a +$200 add-on per PRD §3 X.1.1.
# Host: UniMate's Hostinger VPS (UniMate pays ~$5–20/mo hosting directly; NOT on Sam's Mac).
# To activate:
#   1. UniMate signs the X.1.1 add-on PO
#   2. UniMate provisions N8N on Hostinger (1-click template OR Docker on VPS)
#   3. Sam imports ops/n8n/lead-sync-workflow.json into UniMate's N8N instance
#   4. Sam configures Google Sheets credential against UniMate's Google Workspace
#   5. Sam registers Supabase DB webhook (Supabase Studio → Database → Webhooks) → UniMate's N8N webhook URL
#   6. Smoke test with a seeded lead end-to-end
# The app code (web/) never calls N8N directly — the pipeline lives entirely outside the Next.js runtime.
# N8N_WEBHOOK_URL stays OUT of the web/ env because the app does not hit it. Recorded here only for ops reference.
# Example shape for UniMate's Hostinger N8N webhook:
#   https://unimate-n8n.yourhostingerdomain.com/webhook/atlas-lead-sync

# Make.com (removed in PRD v1.1 — 2026-04-17). See PRD changelog for rationale.
